================================================================================
EPISODE 1: THE ORCHARD
================================================================================

You fly for hours. The branch tugs downward.

Below: two vast orchards, separated by a weathered fence.

To the LEFT: Apple trees in perfect rows. White signs. Clean paths.
"STEVE'S ORCHARD - Premium Experience Guaranteed"

To the RIGHT: Orange trees sprawling wild. Hand-painted signs. Buzzing life.
"ANDY'S GROVE - Open to All"

Dawn's Branch glows faintly. One of these holds what you need.

CHOOSE:
[A] Enter Steve's Apple Orchard (LEFT)
[B] Enter Andy's Orange Grove (RIGHT)
[C] Examine the fence between them
[D] Check your inventory

================================================================================
PATH A: STEVE'S APPLE ORCHARD
================================================================================

You land at the entrance.

A sleek scarecrow stands guard. Silver buttons. Polished staff.
This is STEVE.

STEVE: "Ah. A visitor. How... quaint."
[He looks at your feathers with mild distaste]

STEVE: "Steve's Orchard isn't for everyone.
We maintain certain... standards.
Answer correctly, and you may enter.
Answer incorrectly, and... well."

[He gestures to a pile of confused-looking sparrows huddled by the fence]

STEVE: "The question is simple:

I have five apples on a table.
I take away two.
I cut one of the remaining apples in half.
I give one half to you.
How many apples do I have now?"

ENTER YOUR ANSWER:
> _

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
[THE TRICK - Counterintuitive Element]
- Most readers may answer: 2 (3 apples minus 1 given away)
- Some readers may answer: 2.5 (accounting for the half)
- CORRECT ANSWER: "You have 2 apples. I have half an apple."

The puzzle requires understanding possessive pronouns. Steve asked "How many 
apples do I have"—not "how many are left." The half given to you is NO LONGER 
his.

If you answer wrong:

STEVE: "Incorrect. You're thinking about totals, not ownership.
Try again. But this time, read more carefully.
Who owns what?"

[SECOND CHANCE - same question, user now alerted to trick]
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

STEVE: "Hmm. Adequate."
[The gate swings open with a soft chime]

STEVE: "Welcome to premium quality. Stay on the path.
Don't touch anything. Follow the rules."

---

You enter a grove of identical apple trees.
Every tree is labeled: A1, A2, A3... A47, A48...

The path splits into three directions:
- LEFT path: Sign says "Scenic Route - 47 trees"
- CENTER path: Sign says "Express Path - Membership Required"  
- RIGHT path: Sign says "Service Entrance - Staff Only"

Dawn's Branch glows faintly... toward the CENTER path.

STEVE [calling from behind]: "Oh, the Express Path?
You'll need a Membership Card for that.
Don't have one? Take the Scenic Route like everyone else."

CHOOSE:
[A] Take the LEFT path (Scenic Route)
[B] Attempt the CENTER path anyway
[C] Try the RIGHT path (Service Entrance)
[D] Talk to Steve about Membership
[E] Examine your surroundings more carefully

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
[THE TRICK - Counterintuitive]

If you choose [D]:
STEVE: "Membership? Oh, that's 3 Golden Apples.
You don't have those. Maybe next season."

If you choose [A]:
You walk the Scenic Route.
Tree A1. Tree A2. Tree A3...
This is going to take forever.

Dawn's Seed pulses. STATUS: Warm - 95%
[You're wasting time]

If you choose [B]:
You try to enter the Express Path.
A shimmering barrier blocks you.

SYSTEM: "Membership required. Please subscribe."

If you choose [C]:
You approach the Service Entrance.
A small door, slightly ajar.

STAFF ONLY - No customers beyond this point

CHOOSE:
[A] Enter anyway
[B] Go back

CORRECT PATH: [C] then [A]
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

You slip through the service entrance.

Behind the perfect rows of apple trees... chaos.
Boxes labeled "DEFECTIVE - DO NOT DISPLAY"
Apples with slight blemishes, sorted into "DISPOSAL"
A back path leading directly to the center.

This is the REAL way through.
Steve's "premium experience" is just the front display.

You walk the service path in minutes.

---

You arrive at the CENTER of the orchard.

A massive tree. Silver bark. Apples made of glass.
This is STEVE'S TREE.

STEVE'S TREE: "Ah. You found the service entrance.
Clever. Or cheating. Hard to say."

[The tree drops a single apple]

STEVE'S TREE: "Most birds take the Scenic Route.
They think 'premium' means following the signs.
But you ignored the rules. Interesting."

The apple splits open.
Inside: a choice.

---

THREE CONTAINERS appear:

[A] PLATINUM GLASS - "iJuice Premium™ - The Ultimate Experience"
[B] SILVER CUP - "iJuice Plus™ - Enhanced Formula"  
[C] WOODEN CUP - "Apple Juice - Standard"

STEVE'S TREE: "Choose your refreshment.
Only one leaves with you."

CHOOSE:
> _

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
[THE TRICK - Counterintuitive]

If you choose [A]:
STEVE'S TREE: "Excellent taste. That'll be 3 Golden Apples."

You don't have Golden Apples.

STEVE'S TREE: "Ah. Aspirational, but broke. Try again."

If you choose [B]:
STEVE'S TREE: "Good choice. That'll be 1 Golden Apple."

You don't have Golden Apples.

STEVE'S TREE: "Perhaps... downgrade your expectations?"

If you choose [C]:
STEVE'S TREE: "The... standard option. How... practical."

[A wooden cup fills with simple apple juice]

STEVE'S TREE: "Free, functional, utterly unremarkable.
But it works. I suppose that's what matters."

**ITEM OBTAINED: Apple Juice**
**INVENTORY:**
✓ Dawn's Branch
✓ Dawn's Seed (STATUS: Warm - 90%)
✓ Apple Juice
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

You turn to leave.

The exit is... missing.

Instead: A WHITE WALL with text:

"TO EXIT STEVE'S ORCHARD:
Prove you understand simplicity.

What is the most valuable thing in this orchard?"

STEVE'S TREE [whispers]: "Most say 'the premium apples.'
They stay here forever."

ENTER YOUR ANSWER:
> _

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
[WRONG ANSWERS]
- "The premium apples" → "Incorrect. Locked in perceived value."
- "The tree" → "Incorrect. You worship the surface."
- "The juice" → "Incorrect. You mistake product for purpose."

[CORRECT ANSWER - variations accepted]
- "The exit" / "Leaving" / "Freedom" / "Getting out"

STEVE'S TREE: "...correct.

The most valuable thing is the ability to leave.
A premium cage is still a cage.

You understand. Go."

[The wall dissolves]
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

================================================================================
PATH B: ANDY'S ORANGE GROVE
================================================================================

You land at the entrance.

A cheerful scarecrow waves. Patched overalls. Mismatched buttons.
This is ANDY.

ANDY: "Hey! Welcome! Come on in!"

[He notices you hesitating]

ANDY: "Oh—wait, gotta make sure you're not a bot.
Just answer this real quick:

I'm thinking of a number between 1 and 100.
What is it?"

ENTER YOUR ANSWER:
> _

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
[THE TRICK - Counterintuitive]

[Whatever number you enter]

ANDY: "Oh! That's... not it. It was [random number].
But hey, you TRIED! That's what counts. Come in!"

[The gate swings open]

[THE REAL TRICK: There was no correct answer. Andy just wants to see if you'll 
engage. The "test" is a joke. This teaches you that ANDY'S GROVE doesn't 
gatekeep—it welcomes everyone.]
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

You enter a wild, sprawling grove.

Orange trees everywhere—different sizes, shapes, varieties.
Some labels: "Navel Orange v2.1" "Blood Orange Beta" "Experimental Hybrid"

Paths branch in every direction.

ANDY [walking with you]: "So! You carrying something important?
That seed looks cool. Where you headed?"

CHOOSE:
[A] Tell Andy about the grove
[B] Stay silent, keep walking
[C] Ask Andy about the oranges
[D] Follow Dawn's Branch direction

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
If you choose [A] or [C]:
ANDY: "The grove! Oh man, I've heard of that place.
Super exclusive, right? You gotta meet some Keeper dude?

These oranges? Oh, they're all open-source genetics.
Anyone can grow 'em. Fork 'em. Remix 'em.
That one over there? A user submission. Wild, right?"

[CONNECTIVITY +1 - You engaged in conversation]

If you choose [D]:
You ignore Andy and follow the branch.

Dawn's Branch glows... north.

ANDY: "Oh, strong silent type! Cool cool. I'll just... follow."

[He does. He keeps talking anyway.]
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

You reach a WALL OF WIDGETS.

Not a physical wall—a wall of TEXT OPTIONS:

[Configure your path]
» Battery Saver Mode: Shortest route, minimal features
» Balanced Mode: Standard path, some exploration
» Performance Mode: Longest route, all features unlocked
» Custom Mode: Build your own path

ANDY: "Oh! Path customization! Love this feature.
What's your style?"

CHOOSE:
> _

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
[THE TRICK - Counterintuitive]

- Battery Saver: Gets you through fastest, but you miss items
- Balanced: Medium path, medium rewards
- Performance: Longest path, most side content (wastes time)
- Custom: Lets you configure, but takes FOREVER

OPTIMAL CHOICE: Battery Saver or Balanced (depends on your stats priority)

But here's the trick—there's a HIDDEN option:

If you type: "Andy, which do you recommend?"

ANDY: "Me? Oh, I just use default. Boring, I know.
But hey—defaults exist for a reason, right?"

[HIDDEN OPTION UNLOCKED]
» Default Mode: Fast, reliable, no nonsense

[If you choose this, you save time AND gain VITALITY +1]
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

You arrive at the CENTER of the grove.

A massive orange tree. Hundreds of varieties grafted onto one trunk.
This is ANDY'S TREE.

ANDY'S TREE: "Yoooo! You made it! Want some juice?"

[A BUILD-YOUR-OWN juice station appears]

"Pick your oranges! Pick your add-ins!
Ginger? Mint? Honey? Turmeric? Activated charcoal?
Go wild! Total freedom!"

[Text interface shows 47 customization options]

Dawn's Seed pulses. STATUS: Warm - 85%

CHOOSE:
[A] Customize your juice (opens detailed menu)
[B] Ask for a recommendation
[C] Just take the default
[D] Skip the juice entirely

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
[THE TRICK - Counterintuitive]

If you choose [A]:
[Menu opens with 47 options]

This will take forever.
Dawn's Seed: STATUS: Warm - 80%... 75%...

[If you spend too long here, seed gets colder]

If you choose [B]:
ANDY'S TREE: "Oh! Uh... honestly? The default's pretty good.
I know, I know—boring. But sometimes simple works!"

If you choose [C]:
ANDY'S TREE: "Hah! Smart bird. Default mode activated."

[A wooden cup fills with fresh orange juice]

**ITEM OBTAINED: Orange Juice**
**INVENTORY:**
✓ Dawn's Branch
✓ Dawn's Seed (STATUS: Warm - 85%)
✓ Orange Juice

ANDY'S TREE: "You know what? Most birds customize for HOURS.
You just... took what works. Respect."

[VITALITY +1]

If you choose [D]:
ANDY'S TREE: "Oh... you don't want juice? But... why not?"

CHOOSE RESPONSE:
[A] "I'm in a hurry"
[B] "I don't need it"
[C] "What does it do?"
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

You turn to leave.

ANDY: "Oh! Before you go—wanna see something cool?"

[Path forward is clear and open]
[But ANDY is offering a SIDE QUEST]

ANDY: "I've been working on this new puzzle.
It's like... a logic thing? Wanna try?
Totally optional! But fun!"

Dawn's Seed pulses. STATUS: Warm - 85%

CHOOSE:
[A] "Sure, show me the puzzle"
[B] "No thanks, I need to go"
[C] "Maybe later?"
[D] Just walk away without responding

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
[THE TRICK]
- [A] leads to a 10-minute puzzle side quest (wastes time, seed gets colder)
- [B] or [D] lets you leave immediately
- [C] Andy says "Cool! Come back anytime!" and lets you go

CORRECT CHOICE: [B] or [D] (resist distraction)

If you choose [A]:
[15 minutes of puzzle gameplay later]

ANDY: "Nice! You solved it! Here's a... uh... 
[checks pockets]
...a cool rock I found!"

**ITEM OBTAINED: Cool Rock**
(This does nothing. It's literally just a rock.)

Dawn's Seed: STATUS: Warm - 70%

[You wasted time on a distraction]
[TRANSIENCE -1, STABILITY -1]

If you choose [B] or [D]:
ANDY: "Oh! Yeah, totally get it. Safe travels!"

[You exit the grove efficiently]
[VITALITY +1]
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

